{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The Rock, His work is perfect</b> — an allusion to the attribute of judgment. And Scripture says <b>His work is perfect</b>, because the deed that proceeds from Him is perfect and whole; it will never falter or change forever, for all His ways are justice — they are mercy, and no defect enters into the deed except through judgment. For judgment to El is faithfulness, and there is no wrong in the Rock, and the judgment is righteous and the Rock is upright."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:48.973423251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}